label a0524:
    # --- Day 10: 2025-05-24 ---
    scene bg schoolgym
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    with dissolve_scene_full
    play music dailyfantasy
    window auto
    # CRITIQUE: The pep rally opening is much more restrained than earlier banter-heavy scenes, but it still stacks observational jokes quickly. Pick where the comedy should thin so the darker Act 1 undertow can show.
    "Saturday arrives wearing a school uniform."
    "The school calls it a special pre-midterm review schedule, which is an impressive way to make mandatory Saturday attendance sound like an academic opportunity."
    "The first item on that opportunity is a pep rally."
    "{i}Because nothing prepares a student for exams like being trapped in a gym with a microphone that peaked in 2009.{/i}"
    "Rows of students fill the floor in uneven blocks. Teachers patrol the edges with clipboards, and the air smells like varnished wood, dust, and reluctant school spirit."
    show asahina neut at t21
    show sam neut at t22
    "Asahina finds me near the back before I can decide whether hiding behind the folded volleyball nets counts as strategy."
    "Sam is with her."
    "Not glued to her, exactly. Just close enough that the space between them looks negotiated."
    
    ah "You look like you already gave up."
    
    mc "I am conserving morale for the written portion."
    
    ah "Good luck. The microphone is about to kill whatever is left."
    
    "She says it lightly, but her attention keeps returning to Sam's collar."
    "The corner is folded under."
    "She fixes it with two quick fingers, then immediately pretends she did not do anything tender in public."
    sa "Thanks."
    ah "You were walking around like that."
    ah "Someone had to intervene."
    sa "I appreciate the rescue."
    "Sam's answer is quiet enough that it does not ask the whole gym to notice."
    "Asahina still looks away like the scoreboard has become urgent."
    "{i}Teen love is apparently ninety percent logistics and ten percent looking at anything except each other.{/i}"
    "A teacher's whistle cuts through the gym."
    "The student body produces a collective sound somewhere between obedience and a dying printer."
    "Onstage, a faculty member steps to the microphone and taps it twice."
    "The speakers answer with a sharp pop."
    "{i}Excellent. The microphone has chosen violence.{/i}"
    "The speech begins."
    "It has discipline, effort, pride, and a metaphor about planting seeds that gets away from itself halfway through and starts implying algebra is a vegetable."
    "At some point, everyone is told to believe in their answers."
    "The line gets a few laughs from the back, mostly because everyone knows belief is not going to carry them through chemistry."
    sa "I believe in maybe half of mine."
    ah "That's generous."
    mc "A bold academic platform."
    "The joke dies naturally instead of turning into a sport."
    "The pep rally keeps going. Student council talks about confidence. A teacher warns us not to treat Monday like an ambush, which is rich coming from the institution scheduling exams on a Monday."
    "By the time the applause reaches its third forced resurrection, the back of the gym has become a loose collection of half-awake students negotiating personal space."
    "That is when Tsubaki slips into view near the aisle."
    show asahina neut at t31
    show sam neut at t33
    show tsubaki neut at t32
    "She has a notebook hugged to her chest, a pen tucked behind one ear, and the careful look of someone searching for a place to stand without becoming an inconvenience."
    ts "Oh."
    ts "Hi."
    
    ah "You got stuck here too?"
    
    ts "My class was told attendance would be noticed."
    ts "I thought that meant I should probably be visible somewhere."
    mc "Strategic visibility. Respectable."
    "Tsubaki almost smiles, then catches sight of Sam and pulls the expression back before it can finish."
    ah "Right. Tsubaki, this is Sam."
    ah "Sam, Tsubaki."
    sa "Hey. Nice to meet you."
    ts "Nice to meet you too."
    "Her voice is polite enough to have been proofread."
    sa "Asa mentioned you saw the volleyball poster."
    "Asahina looks at him quickly."
    "Not angry. More exposed than anything."
    ah "I only said she noticed it."
    ts "It was hard not to."
    ts "The colors stood out, and the lettering was clean."
    ts "I liked it."
    "Asahina's grip shifts on her bag strap."
    "She is trying to look casual and failing by exactly the amount that makes it obvious she cares."
    ah "Thanks."
    ah "I mean, I had to redo the title like four times, so...good."
    sa "She was really proud of it."
    ah "Sam."
    "There is a warning in her voice, but not much heat."
    "Tsubaki lowers her eyes to her notebook. For a second, she looks like she has been trusted with something fragile by accident."
    ts "You should be proud."
    ts "It looked like you cared about it."
    "That lands more gently than any joke could."
    "Asahina does not know where to put it."
    "Sam, to his credit, does not rescue her from the silence."
    "The faculty member onstage asks everyone to stand for the closing cheer, and the gym groans upright."
    "Tsubaki ends up beside us because the crowd gives her no cleaner exit."
    "Sam shifts half a step to make room."
    "Asahina notices."
    "Tsubaki notices Asahina noticing."
    "The moment is small, almost nothing."
    # CRITIQUE: This is the right seed for the Asahina/Sam/Tsubaki fault line, but "it feels like something has been introduced" tells the reader how to file it. Let the awkward choreography carry more of the implication.
    "It still feels like something has been introduced that none of us knows how to name."
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    show sam at thide
    hide sam
    show tsubaki at thide
    hide tsubaki
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "The closing cheer happens."
    nier "Nobody is transformed by school spirit, but several people do clap on beat by the end, which probably counts as institutional success."
    nier "The student body pours back into the corridors with the defeated relief of people released from educational weather."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_1
    scene bg corridor
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    "The hallway becomes a moving complaint."
    "Everyone has somewhere to be, nobody wants to be there, and midterms hang over the ceiling lights like a bad forecast."
    show asahina neut at t31
    show tsubaki neut at t32
    show sam neut at t33
    "Tsubaki walks with us until the first stairwell."
    "Her class is supposed to report to a different floor, but the traffic pins us together for one more minute."
    sa "So, Tsubaki, do Saturday review days always feel this illegal?"
    ts "I don't know."
    ts "I try not to rank bad things unless I have to."
    
    ah "That's probably healthy."
    
    sa "Healthier than my system. I rank everything and then get mad at the list."
    "Tsubaki lets out a breath that might have become a laugh if the hallway were quieter."
    ts "That sounds stressful."
    sa "It is, but I like having data."
    "A teacher waves Tsubaki's class toward the stairs."
    ts "I should go."
    ts "It was nice meeting you."
    sa "Same here."
    ah "See you later, maybe."
    ts "Maybe."
    "She gives a small bow and slips into the stairwell current."
    show tsubaki at thide
    hide tsubaki
    show asahina neut at t21
    show sam neut at t22
    "Asahina watches her go for one second too long."
    sa "She seems kind."
    ah "Yeah."
    ah "A little nervous, but...yeah."
    "She says it as if kindness and nervousness are both facts she is filing for later."
    "Then she looks at Sam, and some private calculation softens around the edges."
    ah "Don't be too charming at people."
    sa "I'll try to keep my destructive power contained."
    "That gets a small smile out of her."
    "Not a punchline. Just relief finding a place to sit."
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    show sam at thide
    hide sam
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "The morning review blocks pass with less yelling and more worksheets."
    nier "Civics becomes a diagram of government powers. Biology becomes a list of terms that all sound like they should come with warning labels."
    nier "Lunch is short, the school store runs out of anything good immediately, and by the time the afternoon block arrives, the whole building feels like it is running on borrowed attention."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_2
    scene bg class_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music daily
    "Last period is English."
    "Foreign language English, specifically, which means the class is split between people who know the answer, people who know the answer but cannot pronounce it under pressure, and people hoping the worksheet becomes self-aware and fills itself in."
    show english_teacher neut at t11
    english_teacher "Phones away."
    english_teacher "You will have enough distractions after exams. For the next forty minutes, the only rectangle I want to see is your review sheet."
    "A few students perform the tragic ritual of putting their phones face-down like mourners at a tiny glass funeral."
    "I do the same."
    "Then my phone buzzes against the desk."
    "{i}Naturally.{/i}"
    "I glance at the screen with the kind of stealth that fools nobody except the version of myself who wants to survive."
    "Monika."
    # CRITIQUE: Monika texting during class is a useful crack in her responsible-president image. If this is intentional neediness, let the scene later remember it; otherwise it can read as inconsiderate rather than vulnerable.
    python:
        _phone_messages = [
            phone_msg("them", "Can I borrow you for five minutes before club?"),
            phone_msg("them", "Not an emergency. Just something I wanted to ask without the whole room doing commentary."),
            phone_msg("me", "I'm in English."),
            phone_msg("them", "I know. Sorry. After class? Before everyone gets to the club room?"),
            phone_msg("me", "Yeah, okay."),
            phone_msg("them", "Thank you. And seriously, sorry for the timing."),
        ]
    call phone_text_conversation("Monika", _phone_messages, append=True) from _call_phone_text_conversation_0524_1
    "I lower the phone beneath the edge of the desk."
    "Victory lasts for roughly half a second."
    "Something white bounces off the corner of my review sheet and rolls into the spine of my textbook."
    "Chalk."
    "{i}An analog projectile. Classic.{/i}"
    english_teacher "[player]."
    mc "Yes?"
    english_teacher "Just because you are an honor student does not mean the rules vanish when your phone lights up."
    english_teacher "Phone away. Next one goes on my desk until the bell."
    "The room goes quiet in the deeply unhelpful way classrooms go quiet when someone else has become entertainment."
    mc "Understood."
    "I obey."
    "The chalk sits near my elbow like a warning from a smaller, dustier civilization."
    "For the rest of class, I write every sentence with the focused intensity of someone who has been publicly reminded that projectiles exist."
    show english_teacher at thide
    hide english_teacher
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "English ends with a review packet, three assigned pages, and the teacher reclaiming the chalk like a weapon checked back into evidence."
    nier "I pack quickly, partly because Monika asked me to, and partly because I would like to leave before anyone tries to ask who was texting me."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_3
    scene bg corridor
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    pause 0.5
    play music dailyleisure
    "The hallway outside the club wing is quieter than usual."
    "Saturday school releases students in waves, and this wing belongs to the kind of people who either have club obligations or have made a strange peace with being indoors on a weekend."
    show monika 1a at t11
    "Monika is waiting near the windows with her bag held in both hands."
    "She brightens when she sees me, then immediately looks guilty."
    m "Hey."
    m "Did I get you in trouble?"
    mc "A little chalk-related incident. Nothing fatal."
    m "I'm sorry. I knew you were in class and still sent it."
    "The apology comes too fast to be just manners."
    "She has been carrying it since she hit send."
    mc "It's okay."
    mc "Really. I chose to answer."
    m "Still."
    "She shifts her bag strap."
    "For someone who requested the meeting, she seems suddenly interested in every safe topic that is not the meeting."
    mc "So what did you want to ask?"
    m "Do you have plans tomorrow?"
    m "Actual plans, I mean. Not the vague kind where you sit near a textbook until guilt becomes studying."
    mc "That was most of the plan, yeah."
    m "Then...would you want to study with me at the public library?"
    m "Just the two of us."
    "She adds the last part carefully."
    "Not because the hallway might misunderstand her."
    "Because I might understand her too well."
    m "There's a cafe nearby, too."
    m "I thought we could go after, if we get enough work done."
    mc "Library, then cafe."
    mc "That sounds less like emergency exam prep and more like you had a whole Sunday in mind."
    m "Maybe I did."
    "She tries to smile, but the first attempt is uneven."
    "Monika can speak in front of a room without blinking. Somehow, asking this takes more courage."
    # CRITIQUE: Strong romantic beat. Monika is finally speaking with feeling instead of only cute banter; let MC have a little more emotional response before he answers with logistics.
    mc "Why me?"
    m "Why wouldn't it be you?"
    mc "You're the literature-history-president type."
    mc "I'm useful if you need someone to explain algebra badly until both of us get annoyed."
    m "That is part of it."
    m "You think through problems differently, and I could use that for chemistry and algebra."
    m "But I also..."
    "She stops, and for once she does not turn the pause into a joke."
    m "I wanted some time with you before next week gets swallowed."
    m "The club has been busy. Track is back. Your family has a lot going on."
    m "I know I'm not owed your Sunday, but I missed talking to you without a room waiting for me to be president."
    "The hallway feels too bright for the sentence."
    "I think about the movie theater, her hand catching my sleeve for half a second, the way she keeps making room for me and then pretending she did not."
    "I also think about exams, college pages, Matsuda's apology, Asahina watching Tsubaki walk away."
    "There are too many things asking for future versions of me."
    "Monika is asking for tomorrow."
    mc "Okay."
    m "Okay?"
    mc "Yeah."
    mc "Library tomorrow. Cafe after."
    mc "Eleven?"
    m "Eleven."
    "Relief reaches her face before she can organize it into something smaller."
    m "Thank you."
    mc "You don't have to thank me for wanting to study."
    m "I wasn't only thanking you for studying."
    "A door opens farther down the hall."
    "Voices from the club room drift toward us, and the moment folds itself away before either of us has to decide what it is."
    m "We should go in."
    mc "Yeah."
    show monika at thide
    hide monika
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    scene bg club_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    play sound moddooropen
    "The club room is almost suspiciously normal."
    "Desks sit where desks should. The closet is closed. Nobody is yelling about metaphor ethics or revenue streams."
    show hikari neut at t31
    show homura neut at t32
    show monika 1a at t33
    "Hikari and Homura are at the front desk comparing notes with the intensity of two people trying not to re-open a previous argument by accident."
    hikari "I changed the ending."
    hikari "Not because I thought you were completely right. Just...because one more line helped."
    homura "I think it does help."
    homura "The image breathes more now."
    hikari "Okay."
    hikari "Good."
    "They both look embarrassed by the peace, which is how I know it is real."
    m "Looks like everyone's surviving Saturday."
    "Club settles into the kind of activity that makes Monika look quietly victorious."
    "People read. People annotate. A pen gets borrowed and returned before the owner has to experience grief."
    "For half an hour, Saturday school forgets to be insulting."
    show hikari at thide
    hide hikari
    show homura at thide
    hide homura
    show monika at thide
    hide monika
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Monika moves from desk to desk with gentle corrections. Hikari rewrites two lines without declaring war. Homura writes feedback that has clearly been checked for sharp edges."
    # CRITIQUE: This is a strong way to dramatize MC's anxiety through club work. Consider actually showing one line of the vending-machine poem; it would answer several earlier "show the writing" comments.
    nier "I work through a short poem about a vending machine that refuses coins and discover, too late, that I have accidentally written about college admissions."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_4
    scene bg club_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    show monika 1a at t11
    with wipeleft_scene
    "Near the end, Monika stops by my desk."
    m "The vending machine is still refusing coins?"
    mc "With conviction."
    m "This image is good."
    # CRITIQUE: This feedback about telling the reader what the machine means should be applied to the script itself. Several scenes explain their subtext one line after successfully showing it.
    m "But the last line tells me what the machine means before I get to decide whether I trust it."
    mc "Let the machine incriminate itself."
    m "Pretty much."
    "She smiles."
    "Normal club smile."
    "President smile."
    "Then her eyes flick to mine for one extra beat."
    "Tomorrow sits there between us, unannounced."
    m "Eleven."
    mc "I remember."
    "She moves on before the word can turn into anything else."
    show monika at thide
    hide monika
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Club ends normally."
    nier "Students leave in small groups, Saturday finally starts to act like Saturday, and I make it home with review packets, tomorrow's plan, and one tiny chalk mark still living on the corner of my bag."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_5
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    pause 1.0
    scene bg kitchen
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_evening zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music fantasyserenity
    "Dinner has the rare energy of everyone being home at the same time."
    "Mom is at the stove. Asahina is setting plates with the air of someone performing compulsory community service."
    "I am assigned cups, which is a responsibility suited to my current leadership level."
    show mom neut at t31
    show asahina neut at t33
    "Mom looks over her shoulder as I put the last cup down."
    mom "How was the pep rally?"
    mc "It was a pep rally on a Saturday before midterms."
    mc "So, spiritually complicated."
    ah "They made us chant about doing our best."
    ah "I could feel my soul leaving."
    mom "I am sorry for your loss."
    "That is the only joke the table needs."
    "Mom plates dinner and sets the pan on a folded towel."
    "Rice, vegetables, chicken, enough sauce to make the whole table smell like someone with competence was involved."
    mom "Were you with Sam?"
    ah "Some of the time."
    "Asahina's answer is careful."
    "Not dishonest. Just arranged."
    mom "And?"
    ah "And nothing. He was normal."
    ah "He made fun of the assembly like everyone else and didn't do anything weird."
    mc "He met Tsubaki."
    ah "She was standing right there."
    ah "It wasn't some event."
    "She says it too quickly."
    "Then she notices she said it too quickly and gets annoyed with herself."
    mom "Tsubaki is Matsuda's friend from the rooftop?"
    mc "Yeah."
    ah "She's nice."
    ah "I mean, quiet, but not in a rude way."
    ah "She complimented the poster again, and I didn't know what to say because she sounded like she actually meant it."
    "Mom's expression softens by a degree."
    mom "It is difficult when someone gives you a compliment you cannot dismiss."
    ah "I can dismiss lots of things."
    mom "I have noticed."
    "Asahina pokes at her rice."
    "The defensiveness stays, but it loses some of its armor."
    ah "Sam was nice to her too."
    ah "Not, like, weird nice. Just normal nice."
    mc "You said nice three times."
    ah "Because that is the word."
    mom "Sometimes it is."
    mom "Nice is not a problem by itself."
    mom "But people who are good at being liked can make it hard to notice what else they are good at."
    "Asahina looks up."
    ah "Are you warning me?"
    mom "I am reminding you that attention feels good, and feeling good is not the same thing as being safe."
    # CRITIQUE: The warning is important, but it is thesis-level explicit. A concrete example or a sharper pause before/after would make it feel like parenting rather than authorial theme delivery.
    mom "That applies to boys, friends, teachers, adults, everyone."
    "The table goes quiet."
    "Not angry quiet."
    "The kind where the joke would be easier, and nobody reaches for it."
    ah "I know."
    "She says it like she wants that to be enough."
    "Mom lets it stand."
    mom "Good."
    "Dinner moves again after that."
    "Not all the way back to easy, but close enough to breathe."
    ah "So why are you going out tomorrow?"
    mc "Monika asked me to study at the public library."
    ah "And then a cafe."
    mc "You were listening."
    ah "You are not subtle."
    ah "Neither is she, honestly."
    mom "Will you be back for dinner?"
    mc "Probably. Library at eleven, cafe after. I don't think it'll be late."
    mom "Text me if plans change."
    mc "I will."
    ah "For the record, I am choosing not to say the obvious thing."
    mc "Thank you for your restraint."
    ah "It hurts."
    "Mom hides a smile behind her glass."
    "This time, I let her have it."
    show mom at thide
    hide mom
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Dinner wanders through safer nonsense after that."
    nier "Asahina reports that one of her classmates tried to use the pep rally banner as a blanket. Mom explains, with alarming specificity, why that is a liability issue. I contribute by eating vegetables and refusing to provide my sister with tomorrow's romantic surveillance schedule."
    nier "For a Saturday stolen by school, the evening manages to feel like a weekend again."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_6
    scene bg bedroom
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_night zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    pause 0.5
    "Night finds me at my desk with English review open, algebra notes stacked beside it, and the dangerous confidence of someone who thinks organizing paper counts as studying."
    "My bag sits on the floor with the chalk mark still visible."
    "{i}A scar of academic law enforcement.{/i}"
    "I am halfway through a sentence about irregular verbs when my door opens without knocking."
    play sound moddooropen
    show asahina neut at t11
    ah "You."
    
    mc "That is technically correct."
    ah "Did you move my charger?"
    ah "The good one. The one that doesn't die if you breathe near the cord."
    mc "I have not touched your charger."
    ah "You borrowed it last week."
    mc "And returned it last week."
    ah "That is exactly what someone hiding evidence would say."
    "She is trying to make it an accusation, but the edges are too tired."
    "The doorway light catches the crease between her eyebrows."
    "Not anger, not really."
    "Just the particular frustration of a person who has misplaced one small thing after a long day full of larger things she cannot organize."
    mc "Asa."
    mc "I seriously don't know where it is."
    ah "Great."
    ah "Cool."
    ah "My phone's at four percent, Sam is texting me about tomorrow's practice schedule, and my room apparently ate copper wiring."
    mc "You can use mine."
    ah "I don't want to use yours."
    mc "Because accepting help from me violates your code?"
    
    ah "Because yours is slow."
    
    "There it is."
    "The joke is small, but it gives her somewhere to put the stress."
    "From downstairs, mom's voice carries up."
    mom "Asahina, your charger is on the kitchen counter."
    "Asahina freezes."
    mc "The house confesses."
    ah "Why is it down there?"
    
    mom "Because you plugged it in while helping with plates and then walked away."
    ah "...I remembered doing that."
    mc "When?"
    ah "Eventually."
    "She steps into the room anyway and leans against the doorframe instead of leaving."
    ah "Sorry."
    # CRITIQUE: This is the better shape for comedy: a fake fight exposes real stress, then the apology gives the scene a second layer. Use this model more often.
    "It comes out fast."
    "Too fast for a normal charger dispute."
    mc "For the charger thing?"
    ah "For yelling before I checked."
    ah "And for being weird at dinner."
    mc "You weren't that weird."
    ah "You don't have to lie. I was very obviously weird."
    "I push the English packet aside."
    # CRITIQUE: MC's summary of Asahina's stress is accurate but a little too counselor-clean for siblings mid-argument. One concrete observation from dinner would make the insight feel earned rather than diagnosed.
    mc "You met a person you might actually like, while standing next to a person you very obviously like, while mom and I keep acting like your whole life needs a caution label."
    mc "A little weird is allowed."
    ah "That was too many words, but...thanks."
    "She looks down the hallway, toward the stairs, then back at me."
    ah "Don't make the Monika thing weird tomorrow."
    mc "I thought you were choosing restraint."
    ah "I used it up at dinner."
    mc "I'll try not to make it weird."
    ah "Good."
    ah "Because she likes you, and you get stupid when someone is direct with you."
    mc "That is a brutal assessment from someone who just accused me over a charger."
    ah "I stand by the pattern, not the evidence."
    "She backs toward the hall."
    ah "Night."
    mc "Night, Asa."
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    play sound moddoorclose
    "The door closes."
    "Downstairs, a drawer opens and shuts."
    "A minute later, Asahina's footsteps cross back toward her room."
    "The house settles again, but not exactly where it was before."
    $ update_character_thought("monika", "Monika asked me to study with her at the public library tomorrow, then go to a cafe afterward. She said she wanted time with me before next week gets swallowed. That is harder to file away as just studying.")
    $ update_character_thought("asahina", "Asa was close to Sam during the pep rally in that intensely teenage way she will deny under oath. She also noticed Tsubaki's kindness and did not know what to do with it.")
    $ update_character_thought("tsubaki", "Tsubaki met Sam today. He was friendly in that effortless way of his, and she got quiet in a way I could not quite place.")
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "The rest of Saturday ends with review packets, a recovered charger, and tomorrow's library plan written on a sticky note I put on my desk so I cannot pretend to forget."
    nier "I check both alarms."
    nier "Then, because growth is not always dramatic, I put my phone on the other side of the room."
